  "chapter": {
    "number": 58,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(59) For the end. Destroy not: by David for a memorial, when Saul sent, and watched his house to kill him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me from my enemies, O God; and ransom me from those that rise up against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, and save me from bloody men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For, behold, they have hunted after my soul; violent men have set upon me: neither is it my iniquity, nor my sin, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Without iniquity I ran and directed my course aright: awake to help me, and behold.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And you, Lord God of hosts, the God of Israel, draw near to visit all the heathen; pity not any that work iniquity. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall return at evening, and hunger like a dog, and go round about the city.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, they shall utter a voice with their mouth, and a sword is in their lips; for who, say they, has heard?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, Lord, will laugh them to scorn; you will utterly set at nothing all the heathen.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "will keep my strength, looking to you; for you, O God, are my helper.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As for my God, his mercy shall go before me: my God will show me vengeance on my enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Slay them not, lest they forget your",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 106
          },
          {
            "text": "law; scatter them by your power; and bring them down, O Lord, my defender.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the sin of their mouth, and the word of their lips, let them be even taken in their pride.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And for their cursing and falsehood shall utter destruction be denounced: they shall fall by the wrath of utter destruction, and shall not be; so shall they know that the God of Jacob is Lord of the ends of the earth. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall return at evening, and be hungry as a dog, and go round about the city.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall be scattered hither and there for meat; and if they be not satisfied, they shall even murmur.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I will sing to your strength, and in the morning will I exult in your mercy; for you have been my supporter, and my refuge in the day of my affliction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You are my helper; to you, my God, will I sing; you are my supporter, O my God, and my mercy.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 106,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "some read λαοῦ 'people'.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 58,
          "verse": 11
        }
      }
    ]
  },
